INFO  2026-06-28 07:41:08,385 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:740 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_authentication_mode:none	- The authentication mode for client requests made to the Iceberg catalog. Choose from: `none`, `bearer`, `oauth2`, and `aws_sigv4`. In `bearer` mode, the token specified in `iceberg_rest_catalog_token` is used unconditonally, and no attempts are made to refresh the token. In `oauth2` mode, the credentials specified in `iceberg_rest_catalog_client_id` and `iceberg_rest_catalog_client_secret` are used to obtain a bearer token from the URI defined by `iceberg_rest_catalog_oauth2_server_uri`. In `aws_sigv4` mode, the same AWS credentials used for cloud storage (see `cloud_storage_region`, `cloud_storage_access_key`, `cloud_storage_secret_key`, and `cloud_storage_credentials_source`) are used to sign requests to AWS Glue catalog with SigV4.In `gcp` mode Redpanda will use VM metadata for authentication.
